1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:04,340
Another critical element of the board effectiveness is

2
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:06,660
the board evaluation that I have just briefly

3
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:07,300
described.

4
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:08,740
And what is that process?

5
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:12,060
The process sees the board appointing a consultant.

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,980
Sometimes some boards decide to do this by

7
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:17,660
themselves but I can assure you that this

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:20,580
is not as effective as appointing a consultant.

9
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:24,060
Indeed, the codes of corporate governance require that

10
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:28,020
the board appoints an external consultant to do

11
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,100
this periodically.

12
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:32,160
For some of the regulated entities, the frequency

13
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:33,160
is annual.

14
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:36,000
For some others, they are allowed to do

15
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,960
this in a three-year circle.

16
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:40,760
So what is being evaluated?

17
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,780
The structure and composition of the board is

18
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:43,480
being evaluated.

19
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:46,180
The operations and effectiveness of the board is

20
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:46,880
being evaluated.

21
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:50,180
The board's oversight of strategy and risk management

22
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:51,340
as well as compliance.

23
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:55,660
The board's oversight of transparency and disclosure as

24
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:57,980
well as the board's oversight of the corporate

25
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,660
citizenship of the entity.

26
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:01,700
So what happens at the end of the

27
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,420
day is that all of these indices that

28
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:09,520
are evaluated, the consultants will identify the areas

29
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:12,000
of strength, the areas of compliance and the

30
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,400
areas of gap that need to be ameliorated

31
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,060
by the board.

32
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:19,100
The consultants will also make recommendations on how

33
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:22,940
these gaps identified can be bridged and the

34
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:26,540
board will then thereafter have an implementation plan

35
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:31,780
that will see it's implementing the recommendations that

36
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:34,580
the consultant has made to fill the gaps.

37
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:38,160
As we round off, we identify or go

38
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:41,160
into the areas, the red flag areas that

39
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:45,440
indicate that the board is veering towards ineffectiveness.

40
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:48,600
If the board has an opaque director selection

41
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,660
process whereby it's not clear to onlookers how

42
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:56,200
the board appoints or selects directors, if the

43
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,600
chair of the board is ineffective, if the

44
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,740
chair of the board is overbearing or the

45
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:04,020
CEO themselves are overbearing, if you have ineffective

46
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:06,220
or dysfunctional directors and the board doesn't have

47
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:09,080
a clear path to existing directors from the

48
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:12,860
board, if meetings lack focus, so if the

49
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:16,180
board directors attend a board meeting and there

50
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:19,720
isn't sufficient clarity on what exactly the board

51
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,540
was trying to achieve, that is a sign

52
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,280
of ineffectiveness and is a major red flag.

53
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:28,240
If there is a poor manual reporting system

54
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:31,380
that leads to information asymmetry so that the

55
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:34,160
executives know much more about the business than

56
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,520
the board does, there's clearly a problem.

57
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,840
If meetings are time-wasting, so the agenda

58
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:44,940
is overloaded, very unclear or loaded with matters

59
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:46,700
that shouldn't even concern the board at all.

60
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:49,600
If the committee system is ineffective, so we've

61
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:54,260
described effective committees, so sometimes boards have committees

62
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:56,920
just to fulfil all righteousness and the committees

63
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:59,400
come to the board with recommendations based on

64
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:02,160
their findings or their deliberations and the board

65
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:04,480
re-opens the matters that it has delegated

66
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:07,400
to the committees, then really and truly the

67
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,080
committee system is ineffective.

68
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:12,200
Where there is groupthink, meaning that there isn't

69
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:15,980
sufficient diversity on the board, then that's also

70
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:16,620
a red flag.

71
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:18,920
So for instance you have an all-male

72
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:20,680
board, or I dare say an all-female

73
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,420
board, even though that is not a very

74
00:03:22,420 --> 00:03:24,820
common occurrence in this part of the world.

75
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:27,180
But if you have a board, for instance,

76
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,320
maybe it's a board with a bank and

77
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:32,000
all the directors are bankers or people with

78
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,760
financial services experience, then that board is likely

79
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,940
to be ineffective because it's not a true

80
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:43,060
representation of the society that really and truly

81
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,100
the bank is serving.

82
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:47,560
If the secretariat is ineffective, because the secretariat,

83
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:51,360
the committee secretary has a critical role to

84
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:53,560
play in board effectiveness, so if the secretariat

85
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:57,140
is ineffective, it is most likely to impact

86
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:59,120
on the board's effectiveness itself.

87
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:01,660
We mentioned tenure for directors, so where you

88
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:04,000
have on-tenure directors, meaning that the board

89
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,360
doesn't have sufficient opportunity to replenish itself or

90
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:11,220
to refresh its membership, then that's also a

91
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:11,720
red flag.

92
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:14,700
Where succession planning is not in place, and

93
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:16,839
this is not just succession planning at the

94
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:20,440
level of management or the other members of

95
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:23,380
the organisation, but succession planning even at the

96
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:24,000
level of the board.

97
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:26,140
So for instance, the board doesn't have a

98
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:30,220
clear path to selecting a replacement for an

99
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:34,100
existing chair, that is a recipe for failure.

100
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:36,740
Or where there isn't a clear path as

101
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:39,680
to how disputes will be resolved, because the

102
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,060
human beings, the individuals, like I said earlier

103
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,580
on, they come onto the board with their

104
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:46,900
own ego, their own background, so occasionally they

105
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,600
are bound to the friction, they are bound

106
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,260
to the conflict.

107
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:51,300
So if the board doesn't have a clear

108
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:53,900
path to how these conflicts or disputes are

109
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:58,740
resolved, it's also a clear path to failure.

110
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:01,680
Where the board is too large or too

111
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,640
small, recall that I said that the Nigerian

112
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:07,340
Code of Corporate Governance does not specify a

113
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:10,380
minimum or maximum number of directors, but the

114
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:12,880
board, in its wisdom, should be able to

115
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:14,660
determine that this is the right size.

116
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:19,620
But the other guidelines, the other corporate governance

117
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:25,160
guidelines, especially the CBN guidelines, actually specifies a

118
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:26,640
maximum and a minimum number.

119
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:28,460
Where the board is too large or too

120
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:31,080
small, it can also impact on its effectiveness,

121
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:33,820
because if it's too small, you then have

122
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:37,360
the probability of a dominant personality on the

123
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:37,600
board.

124
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:40,660
Where the board is made up of directors

125
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:42,460
that are only looking out for their own

126
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:47,020
interests, especially where they don't declare such interests.

127
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,880
And finally, where the board doesn't have a

128
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:53,600
performance management mechanism, either for measuring its own

129
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:57,260
performance, but more especially for measuring the performance

130
00:05:57,260 --> 00:06:00,240
and giving feedback through management.
